# NativMix Platform Guardrails

## Communication and code language
- Communicate with the user in German.
- Keep source code and code comments in English.

## Wayland-safe integration
- Do not use window-scraping tools like `wmctrl` or `xdotool`.
- Use audio-server data for stream detection instead of window inspection.
- Keep Wayland app integration via `setproctitle` and `setDesktopFileName`.

## Theming and autostart
- Read system theme and color preferences through XDG Desktop Portal (`org.freedesktop.portal.Settings`).
- Do not hardcode KDE/GNOME-specific paths for theming.
- Autostart must be user-space only via `~/.config/autostart/`.
- Never use `sudo` or runtime writes to `/etc/xdg/autostart/`.

## Audio safety behavior
- Keep two-stage mute-catch for new streams:
  1) Immediately mute or set safe low volume on `new`.
  2) Resolve metadata on `change`, apply mapped channel volume, then unmute.
